Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::sending_a_command_is_total_against_any_controller`.

The defect: a response timeout is reported as a bad response, so an empty slot reads as a card
with a failing CRC, and identification takes the wrong branch (it tells an eMMC from an SD card by
which command goes unanswered).

Expected to fail: the assertion that a `BadResponse` carries `RCRC` or `RE`, on a status with only
`RTO` set.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
@@ -486,7 +486,7 @@
             return Err(Error::CommandTimeout(command.index, status));
         }
         if status & registers::RINTSTS_RTO != 0 {
-            return Err(Error::NoResponse(command.index));
+            return Err(Error::BadResponse(command.index, status));
         }
         if status & (registers::RINTSTS_RCRC | registers::RINTSTS_RE) != 0 {
             return Err(Error::BadResponse(command.index, status));
